vcam.ko -- provenance and third-party material
==============================================

Original work (GPL-2.0)
-----------------------
Everything under src/, include/, host/, shim/, tools/, scripts/, plus README.md,
BUILD-KO.md and verify/ioctl_abi_check.c, is an independent implementation and
released under the GNU General Public License version 2 (see LICENSE).

It contains no vendor source code. The behaviour it reproduces (a frame
injection pool, the pose rule, the play-range gate, the format gating and the
ownership rules) was derived from observing a locally-owned sample; only public
kernel interfaces are used at runtime.

Third-party files kept verbatim
------------------------------
verify/linux-asm-generic-ioctl.h
    From the Linux kernel: include/uapi/asm-generic/ioctl.h.
    License: GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note (SPDX header retained in the file).
    Purpose: the authoritative definition the module's portable ioctl encoding
    is statically asserted against.

verify/kmi_*.txt
    GKI ABI symbol lists from AOSP's kernel/common
    (android/abi_gki_aarch64_generic, _qcom, _mtk, _virtual_device, and the
    vendor delta lists _oplus and _xiaomi, for the android13-5.10,
    android14-6.1 and android15-6.6 branches).
    License: GPL-2.0 (Linux kernel / ACK).
    Purpose: check that the module's kernel symbol surface stays inside the GKI
    KMI, i.e. that a plain out-of-tree kbuild works without patching modpost.

Build-method references (not included, credited)
-----------------------------------------------
KernelSU   https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU
    Cross-checked for how a loadable kernel module is built per KMI
    (.github/workflows/ddk-lkm.yml, kernel/Makefile, kernel/build-all.sh) and
    for the compatibility options such a build needs.

DDK        https://github.com/5ec1cff/ddk
    The tool that supplies the per-KMI prepared GKI kernel trees, clang
    toolchain and kbuild environment used by those builds. No DDK files are
    redistributed here; BUILD-KO.md only documents how to use it.

Android Common Kernel / AOSP   https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common
    Source of the GKI ABI files listed above.
